{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R3"],
      "pins": ["R3.1", "R3.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "RST"],
      "obs": "R3 is drawn as 10 (ohms) between the +5V rail and the RST global label (which feeds MCU pin 1, J1.4 and J4.5). It is the only element holding the reset line high, i.e. the reset pull-up.",
      "expected": "A reset pull-up should be in the 10 kΩ range, consistent with the other pull-ups on this sheet (R1 = 10K gate pull-up, R6 = 10K TACH pull-up). A 10 Ω pull-up is three orders of magnitude too low.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R3 10 between +5V and RST (sheet /, page 1, top centre)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R1 10K and R6 10K used as pull-ups elsewhere on the same sheet"}
      ],
      "impact": "The reset line is stiffly tied to +5V through 10 Ω; any device that pulls RESET low (e.g. the ISP programmer on J4, or a transient) forces ~0.5 A through R3, and the intended high-impedance pull-up behaviour is lost. This is a deviation from the reference pull-up value.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.3", "U1.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "VCC"],
      "obs": "On the right tile, U1 (LM1117-5.0) pin 3 (VI, input) and pin 2 (VO, output) are both wired to the +5V arrow; the VCC net (the raw supply from J5, decoupled by C1) does not reach the regulator input.",
      "expected": "The LM1117-5.0 input (VI) must be connected to the unregulated VCC supply so it can generate the +5V rail; tying VI to VO bypasses the regulator and leaves +5V without a source.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 LM1117-5.0, pin 3 VI and pin 2 VO both to +5V (sheet /, right tile, top)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "VCC net appears only at J5.2, C1 and JP1.2, not at U1.VI"}
      ],
      "impact": "If this reading is correct, the +5V rail is never powered from VCC and the MCU (whose pin 8 is tied to +5V) would not start. Lower confidence because the input arrow label is hard to disambiguate from VCC at this resolution.",
      "confidence": 0.25
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing supports at least one deviation: the reset pull-up R3 is 10 Ω instead of the ~10 kΩ used for every other pull-up on the sheet (R1, R6), which is three orders of magnitude off; a possible second issue is the LM1117 input pin tied to +5V rather than VCC, though that reading is less certain."
}

